'''Ototo Corps''' (オトート開発隊, ''Otōto Kaihatsu-tai'', '''Ototo Corps''') is a feature introduced in the [[Version 6.0 Update]]. This feature allows the player to develop a new appearance for the [[Cat Base]], [[Cat Cannon]] attacks and also further increase the Cannon's power. Ototo Corps can be accessed by scrolling to the right in the [[Gamatoto Expedition|GAMATOTO]] screen.

==Explanation==
Ototo Corps is unlocked after clearing [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1 and is only functional after the player has upgraded the Cat Cannon Power, Range and Charge to level 10 at the [[Upgrade Menu]]. To develop, GAMATOTO's brother '''Ototo''' requires some resource materials and engineers to build.

Materials can be obtained randomly when clearing stages in [[Stories of Legend]], [[Uncanny Legends]] or [[Zero Legends]]. They can also be obtained from [[Heavenly Tower]], [[Legend Quest]], certain [[Gauntlet]]s, or the [[Builder's Blitz Stages]].

The engineer(s) required can be obtained from GAMATOTO Expedition randomly after clearing an expedition, one at a time with a maximum of having five engineers. When firing a GAMATOTO helper, the players also has the option to turn them into an engineer instead of sending them home.

Note that when in progress of upgrading, you may still obtain engineers from GAMATOTO Expeditions.<!-- Insert image here: Access the Ototo Page by sliding to right from GAMATOTO Expedition Screen -->

==Obtaining Materials==
:''For a complete list of material drop rates, see [[Ototo Corps/Item Drop Rates]].''

Materials are scattered throughout Legend Stages. Upon clearing any stage, there is a chance to get materials. There are 8 types of materials in Stories of Legend and Uncanny Legends: Bricks, Feathers, Coal, Sprockets, Gold, Meteorite, Beast Bones, and Ammonite. They are each associated with a certain trait ([[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]], [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]], [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]], respectively). The type of material dropped is not directly affected by enemies in that level; for example, Feathers can be received in levels that don't spawn any Floating enemies at all. Materials won't drop in most [[Special Events|Event Stages]] (red), [[Collaboration Events]] (purple) and [[Enigma Stages]] (lime). No levels have a limit to how many materials can be obtained or how many times they will drop, so the player could theoretically just grind one stage forever. [[Torture Room]] is an effective stage for this since it's so quick, and every material drops there except Meteorite and Ammonite.

Each sub-chapter has a set percentage for each material to drop and a parameter for the number of times to apply the percentages. These are applied on all stages in a sub-chapter, so it's always more efficient to farm a stage with the lowest [[Cat Energy|energy]] cost. A higher Crown difficulty generally increases the number of cycles to choose, thus effectively increasing the likelihood of obtaining materials and increasing the maximum material drop count. Crown difficulty does not directly change the drop rates. For example, [[The Legend Begins]] in 1-Crown has 2 cycles and there is a 13% chance each for bricks, coal, and sprockets. When a stage in this sub-chapter is cleared, 2 cycles will be held. A cycle will determine one of the possible materials or none. In this case, bricks, coal, and sprockets will be chosen at a 13% chance and there is a 61% chance for nothing to drop in each cycle. The materials will drop more frequently than the percentages in actual gameplay because the percentages in the data don't account for the number of cycles. Some of the recommendations below for material farming contain lower percentages. This is because some players may not be able to consistently complete later stages that are more difficult, or simply haven't reached these stages yet.
*{{1c}} gives a maximum of 3 items.
*{{2c}} gives a maximum of 4 items.
*{{3c}} and {{4c}} give a maximum of 5 items.
The best sub-chapters to gain each material:
*Bricks - [[Sushi Island]] (25%), [[Glucosamine Desert]] (27%)
*Feathers - [[Risqué Terrain]] (16%), [[Moodist Beach]] (21.32%), [[Laboratory of Relics]] (22%)
*Coal - [[Squishy Cave]] (19.51%), [[Capone's Jail]] (24%)
*Sprockets - [[The Legend Begins]] (13.33%), [[Quarantine Isles]] (13.73%), [[Diver's City]] (25.38%)
*Gold - [[Grotesque Gallery]] (14.72%), [[Pararila Peninsula]] (16.75%)
*Meteorite - [[Area 22]] (33%), [[Beyond the Savannah]] (32%)
*Beast Bones - [[Walk of Fame]] (32%)
*Ammonite - [[Here Be Dragons]] (23.65%), [[Abyss Gazers]] (27%), [[Drunken Foundry]] (33.99%)

Drop rates for materials per sub-chapter have a trend of matching the traits of enemies found in its stages. For example, Area 22 has a high drop rate for Meteorites and Suburbs of the Dead has a high drop rate for Beast Bones, as both sub-chapters feature a heavy presence of Alien and Zombie enemies, respectively.

It should be noted that through normal play Bricks, Feathers, Coal, Gold and Ammonite are not usually limiting factors in base development, leaving Sprockets, Beast Bones and Meteorite as the more likely bottlenecks. Especially in early-mid Stories of Legend, where Beast Bones and Meteorite are hard to come by, getting the materials necessary may prove difficult. Thankfully, each has a relatively quick farming stage, those being [[Earthshaker]], [[Paparazzi Paradise]] or [[Beverly Hills Scoop]], and [[Tunguska Event]], respectively. Note that these stages are more energy-efficient on {{3c}} and {{4c}} due to the increased material drop cap.

Zero Legends stages drop a new set of 8 materials called '''Extra-Dimensional Materials''', each being a "Z" version of one of the original materials. These materials are used to upgrade Foundation and Style components of the Cat Base. In addition to drops in Zero Legends, they can also be obtained by spending 5 of the original material and an engineer to merge 1 Extra-Dimensional material in an hour (after completing [[Eldritch Forces]]). Due to the need to use 1 Engineer to create 1 Extra-Dimensional material, it is recommended to grind the materials from Zero Legends if it is unlocked. However, the only way to obtain Ammonite Z currently is from merging, as they do not drop in the existing Zero Legends stages. Note that Zero Legends has a maximum of 4 materials, unlike Stories of Legend and Uncanny Legends. This is because Zero Legends stages are currently limited to {{2c}} at most.

The best sub-chapters to gain each material:
*Bricks Z - [[Reverse Royal Grave]] (16%), [[Candy Paradise]] (16.75%), [[Garden of Wilted Thoughts]] (19.71%)
*Feathers Z - [[Cats of a Common Sea]] (16.24%), [[En Garde Shrine]] (19.71%)
*Coal Z - [[En Garde Shrine]] (16.75%), [[Forest Playground]] (16.75%), [[Konjac Valley]] (18.27%)
*Sprockets Z - [[Konjac Valley]] (18.27%)
*Gold Z - [[Patisserie Parklands]] (27%), [[The Ururuvu Journals]] (28%)
*Meteorite Z - [[Reverse Royal Grave]] (23%), [[Stratospheric Pathway]] (43%)
*Beast Bones Z - [[Candy Paradise]] (33.5%)

==Getting Engineers==
Engineers can be obtained from GAMATOTO expeditions. Player will be notified when obtaining one. Can be obtained at the same time as an expedition assistant for GAMATOTO. Retiring an expedition assistant also gives the option to change them to an engineer.[[File:Engineer.png|thumb|158x158px]]

The engineer will be spent on base upgrade, and players can have up to 5 at once. Once the limit is reached, no extra engineers can be obtained. Base upgrades can cost from 1-4 engineers.
[[File:Engineer Descriprion.png|thumb|199x199px]]

==Upgrading Tutorial==
To access Ototo Corps, simply go to the GAMATOTO screen and swipe left. This will take you to the Ototo Corps screen. Once on the Ototo Corps screen, tap on the engineer, and select an upgrade. If the required materials are available, development on a project can commence and will finish in 12 or 24 hours.
*You can't upgrade any Cannon past level 10 if your Cat Cannon Attack and Cat Cannon Charge aren't level 20+10.

==Base Upgrade Materials/Information==
Warning: Cancelling the progress will not return engineers or materials used. Progress can be sped up using [[Catamin]]s, just like GAMATOTO expeditions.
{{:Ototo Corps/Base Upgrade Materials}}

==Foundation and Style Upgrades==
After clearing Stories of Legend, each Foundation of the non-default bases can be upgraded for an effect of reducing all deployed Cats' damage taken from a specific trait, and each Style can be upgraded to give Cats [[Special Abilities#Resist|Resistance]] against a specific ability. These effects are only unlocked when each part is upgraded to level 1; just building them will not give any effects in battle. The percentages for effects of all Foundation and Style types begin from 0.75% at level 1 and increase by 0.75% per level up to 15% at level 20. Note that Foundations do not reduce damage taken by the base.

Target Trait resistance and [[Wave Attack|Wave]]/[[Surge Attack|Surge]] resistance can stack: for example, against [[Red EnerG]], with the Waterblast Style and Foundation equipped, his Surge damage would be reduced to 72.25% of his base damage, and direct hit damage to 85%.

