==Tips==
*Foundation/Style/Cannon combinations are saved between formation slots, so double check which Cannon you have equipped if you're making significant changes to a formation.
*For most early stages, the normal Cat Cannon is perfectly capable if not the best choice. It excels at clearing out enemies with very low health (including Assassin Bears at lower strength magnifications but not [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]]), knocks enemies back, and can be used to interrupt an enemy just before they finish a long attack animation, giving the player a bit more time to attack them. Once you've progressed to where the normal Cat Cannon is unable to kill any enemies, you'll want to use something else, except for levels where you can't get around [[Assassin Bear]].
*In the late stages, the Thunderbolt will be a good, safe choice if you don't know what's coming. It is thus recommended to upgrade it at some point.
*The Slow Beam excels at applying a moderate length slow effect to all enemies on the battlefield that aren't immune. It is perfect for keeping fast and powerful enemies from plowing through your defenses, either after your front line is cleared by an enemy attack, or as a means of giving your status effect-inflicting Cat Units more time to do their job.
*The Iron Wall can be used to instantaneously block non-[[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies from advancing for a brief moment, and is most effective against enemies with slower attack rates that do not inflict [[Critical Hit]]s. It is also capable of stalling enemies that are usually immune/highly resistant to the other cannon effects such as Shielded [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies and [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sages]]. Unlike the Slow Beam, the Iron Wall can result in enemies grouping up in front of the wall, which could be a good chance to wipe them out all at once with a powerful Area Attack. However, if your cat limit is full, you cannot use the Iron Wall, because it counts as a cat.
*The Thunderbolt can be used to freeze all enemies in front of the furthest away Cat Unit (closest to the enemy's base) for a moderate duration, in addition to doing slight damage which may be sufficient for wiping out peons. This can delay the action of enemies that have long attack animations without knocking them back, which might be preferable depending on enemy composition. It can also stall enemies so your status-inflicting cats can do their job. Note that it doesn't work on freeze immune enemies.
*The Waterblast can be used to remove a significant percentage of Metal enemies' health in front of the furthest away Cat Unit. As the Waterblast removes health based the target's remaining health and not their maximum health, it is best used against Metals with the largest health pools as early as possible for maximum effect. Never use Waterblast against non-Metal enemies; it will only remove 0.1% of the target's remaining health.
*The Holy Blast is an extremely potent anti Zombie Cannon that removes a percentage of maximum health from all Zombies on the field, in addition to freezing them briefly, knocking them back, forcing burrowed Zombies to the surface (plus dealing significantly increased damage), and permanently killing Zombies who are finished off by the cannon. It is best used to intercept powerful Zombies (such as [[Cadaver Bear]]) who have already burrowed into the ground, or to chip away at and potentially finish off Zombies on the surface (even if they are not z-killed, as its soulstrike will get to chip them). Those with higher health, like Daboo and Z-Onel, can be much more manageable with its presence. Starting at level 20, it is capable of instantly Z-killing the corpses of Daboo and Big Peng Z, who otherwise revive infinitely at 10% HP. While it helps to demolish zombie-heavy stages, it does not have any effect against non Zombies.
*The Breakerblast is a fast-acting shot that quickly knocks back and breaks the Barrier of the nearest enemies. It can be used as an alternative to the Cat Cannon for knocking back and damaging only the enemies in the front, which may be preferable to knocking back all enemies depending on enemy composition. It can also be used to interrupt enemy attacks, and is easier to time due to its more immediate effect. Finally, it is very effective at breaking Barriers in a group of enemies, or one of a single tough enemy that easily obtainable [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breakers]] might struggle with. Note when firing it make sure that there are no burrowed or defeated zombies, as well as KB-immune ones, as the Breakerblast cannon can waste its shot on them.
*The Curseblast is a Curse-type Slow Beam which Curses enemies, but doesn't inflict damage, so only bring it to stages with foes whose abilities can be Cursed. The abilities it affects are Weaken, Freeze, Slow, Knockback, Dodge Attack, Warp, Curse, Toxic and Delay. It is rarely the best choice, but it can reliably stop the nastiest effects, allowing your army to break free from [[Henry]]'s perma-freeze and advance into his blindspot at once, for example.
*Base Foundations give all your units a significant boost in defense against enemies of a given trait. The most notable interaction related to this is that enemies such as Mr. Puffington and the 600% magnification Cadaver Bears in early 3-crown UL who deal 30,000 damage can be tanked by Manic Eraser with the damage reduction effect. Though expensive and essentially not available until ZL, upgrading at least the Curseblast and Holy Blast foundation effects is recommended for players going through 3-crown UL.

