==Trivia==
*Athough Ototo's name sounds like 弟 ''otōto'' (younger brother), he was confirmed to be [[Gamatoto Expedition|GAMATOTO]]'s older brother in [[Nyanko Daisensou ~Nippon Shinryaku Hiroku~]].
*When Ototo Corps was added, 10 was the highest level to which a Cannon could be upgraded. [[Version 6.8 Update|Version 6.8]] raised the cap to 20 for all Cannons, [[Version 9.8 Update|Version 9.8]] made it possible to upgrade Slow Beam, Iron Wall and Thunderbolt to level 30, [[Version 10.1 Update|Version 10.1]] did the same for Waterblast and Holy Blast, [[Version 10.5 Update|Version 10.5]] allowed level 30 for Breakerblast and Curseblast, and [[Version 11.8 Update|Version 11.8]] made it possible to upgrade Normal Base to level 30.
*The Iron Wall Cat, [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Meditation Cat]], [[Cheetah Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cheetah Cat]] and [[Mamoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Mamolan Pasalan]] are the only non-Conjured Cat Units with 0 speed.
*The Iron Wall Cat and Cheetah Cat are the only non-Conjured Cat Units that do not attack.
*Prior to [[Version 12.2 Update|Version 12.2]], the Foundation and Style parts were cosmetic and lacked any upgrades. Only the Cannon (Effect) part changed the effect of the base.
*To fully upgrade all cannons, foundations and styles the following is needed:
**1623 Bricks and 498 Bricks Z
**1124 Feathers and 340 Feathers Z
**1503 Coal and 471 Coal Z
**1105 Sprockets and 273 Sprockets Z
**1035 Gold and 265 Gold Z
**1255 Meteorites and 391 Meteorites Z
**1163 Beast Bones and 310 Beast Bones Z
**234 Ammonites and 112 Ammonites Z
**1202 Engineers and 6684 hours of upgrade time
***The total upgrade time only includes time spent on upgrades, and in practice they'll take far longer, even with reductions from Catamins. Players still need to wait for GAMATOTO to bring back engineers, and likewise waiting for energy or just playing stages also require additional time.
***Due to there currently being no levels where Ammonites Z drop from, an extra 112 hours, 112 engineers and 560 Ammonites are needed for merging. This is subject to change as more levels are added.
* The Waterblast Cannon is similar in appearance to the Pokemon Wailmer.

